JBBind bundles and depends on the following third-party components.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Voronota / voronota-js  —  https://github.com/kliment-olechnovic/voronota
MIT License. Copyright (c) Kliment Olechnovic.

Version 1.29.4781 is compiled into the container and performs the Voronoi
tessellation and all per-atom structural features. JBBind ships a modified
derivative of the repository's `extract-and-describe-receptor-protein` script as
`tools/describe-receptor-chain`; the unmodified original is preserved at
`tools/reference/` and `make diff-tool` prints the delta.

If you publish results produced with JBBind, cite Voronota:
  Olechnovic K, Venclovas C. "Voronota: A fast and reliable tool for computing
  the vertices of the Voronoi diagram of atomic balls." J Comput Chem, 2014.
  Olechnovic K, Venclovas C. "VoroMQA: Assessment of protein structure quality
  using interatomic contact areas." Proteins, 2017.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ESM-2  —  https://github.com/facebookresearch/esm
MIT License. Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.

The `esm2_t33_650M_UR50D` checkpoint is baked into the container and produces the
per-residue sequence embeddings.

  Lin Z, Akin H, Rao R, et al. "Evolutionary-scale prediction of atomic-level
  protein structure with a language model." Science, 2023.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3Dmol.js  —  https://3dmol.csb.pitt.edu/
BSD-3-Clause. Copyright (c) University of Pittsburgh.

Vendored at `jbbind/static/vendor/3Dmol-min.js` so the container renders
structures with no external network access.

  Rego N, Koes D. "3Dmol.js: molecular visualization with WebGL."
  Bioinformatics, 2015.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gemmi  —  https://gemmi.readthedocs.io/    MPL-2.0
PyTorch, PyTorch Geometric, FastAPI, pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn — see
requirements.txt; each retains its own licence.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Training data

The models were trained on structures and interface annotations derived from
PPI3D (https://bioinformatics.lt/ppi3d/) and SAbDab. The trained weights in
`models/` are derivative of that data; check the respective terms before
redistributing them.
